ARM problem
▪To avoid needless computations, it would be useful to prune the extracted rules 
early. 
▪The support of a rule 𝐗⇒𝐘 depends only on the support of the itemset 𝐗∪𝐘. 
o E.g.,
{Butter, Diapers} → {Milk} 
{Butter, Milk} → {Diapers}
{Diapers, Milk} → {Butter} 
{Butter} → {Diapers, Milk} 
{Milk} → {Butter,Diapers} 
{Diapers} → {Butter,Milk}
o If the itemset {Butter, Diapers, Milk} is infrequent, then all the previous rules 
can be pruned immediately without having to compute their confidence values.
18
Have identical support because they 
involve items from the same itemset 
{Butter, Diapers, Milk}.

